<title>USA: Interscience files for bankruptcy.</title>
<headline>Interscience files for bankruptcy.</headline>
<dateline>AGOURA HILLS, Calif. 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interscience Computer Corp said Friday it filed for protection under Chapter 11 of the federal bankruptcy code on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the filing was to allow it to reorganize its operations and improve cash flow. It had cash flow problems in the past year due to four acquisitions. In January, Interscience posted a loss of $1.05 million, or $0.53 a share, for its 1996 fiscal year.</p>
<p>The company said the filing will facilitate the company's resolving several pending lawsuits and emerge from bankruptcy without the suits affecting it's operations.</p>
